# Copy to .env.local (never commit real secrets).

# --- Web ---
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3000

# --- Claude / Agent runtime (Thing 2) ---
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- LLM observability + ROI data (Thing 2) ---
# LANGFUSE_PUBLIC_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_SECRET_KEY=
# LANGFUSE_HOST=https://cloud.langfuse.com

# --- Database: Postgres + pgvector (Thing 4/5) ---
# DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/aihub

# --- Embeddings (Thing 5) ---
# VOYAGE_API_KEY=

# --- Remote MCP servers (Thing 3) ---
# Client systems that expose their own MCP endpoint over Streamable HTTP. Unlike
# the built-in servers (config in code), these are deployment-specific, so they
# are declared here and auto-registered into the control plane on first read.
# `tokenEnv` names another env var holding the bearer token — keep the secret out
# of the JSON blob. Malformed JSON ⇒ no remote servers (fails closed).
# HUB_REMOTE_MCP_SERVERS={"pm-tool":{"url":"http://localhost:3000/api/mcp","label":"PM-tool","description":"Read-only project delivery data: projects, tasks, risks, scope.","tokenEnv":"PM_TOOL_MCP_TOKEN"}}
# PM_TOOL_MCP_TOKEN=

# --- Microsoft 365: the secretary agent's mailbox and calendar ---
# Read-only Mail.Read + Calendars.Read via an app-only (client credentials) app
# registration with admin consent. No user sign-in, no refresh token to rotate.
#
# Application permissions reach EVERY mailbox in the tenant, so scope the
# registration to the secretary alone with an Application Access Policy or this
# secret reads the whole organisation's mail. See docs/secretary-agent.md.
#
# Missing any of the four ⇒ the server exits 1 naming what is missing, and the
# agent run fails loudly rather than reporting an empty inbox.
# M365_TENANT_ID=
# M365_CLIENT_ID=
# M365_CLIENT_SECRET=
# M365_MAILBOX=secretary@yourdomain.com
# Times are rendered in this zone (Windows or IANA name). Defaults to UTC.
# M365_TIMEZONE=Europe/Copenhagen

# --- The scheduler (unattended agent runs) ---
# Off unless set to exactly 1. The consequence of being wrong is an agent acting
# unbidden — a dev container pointed at production's database should not start
# reading someone's mailbox every minute — so production opts in rather than
# development opting out. Safe on several Fly machines: they all tick, and the
# claim in agent_schedules decides which one wins. See docs/schedules.md.
# HUB_SCHEDULER=1

# --- Security / AuthZ ---
# OAuth 2.1, with WorkOS AuthKit as the authorization server. This is the front
# door: it is what lets ChatGPT Enterprise and M365 Copilot enrol the hub as a
# connector, and it is what makes a person a revocable row rather than a secret.
# See docs/auth.md.
#
# The AuthKit origin, which is also the token issuer. Unset ⇒ OAuth is off and
# the hub is reachable by credential only (no enterprise surface can enrol it).
# WORKOS_AUTHKIT_DOMAIN=https://your-app.authkit.app
#
# This server's RFC 8707 resource indicator: the value clients request and the
# `aud` we require. Must match the Resource Indicator configured in the WorkOS
# dashboard exactly. Defaults to <HUB_BASE_URL>/api/mcp.
# HUB_MCP_RESOURCE=https://hub.example.com/api/mcp
#
# Public origin, used for redirects and to derive the resource indicator.
# HUB_BASE_URL=https://hub.example.com

# --- Knowledge access (increment 02) ---
# How a collection nobody has classified is treated. `open` (the default) keeps
# an existing corpus readable the moment this deploys; `restricted` means
# nothing is readable without an explicit grant in /admin → Knowledge.
#
# The default is a migration affordance, not a policy. Classify everything, then
# set this to `restricted`. See docs/knowledge-access.md.
# HUB_DEFAULT_COLLECTION_VISIBILITY=restricted

# --- Security / AuthZ: the deprecated token map -----------------------------
# REPLACED by per-principal credentials issued from /admin (`hub_sk_…`), which
# are revocable without a deploy and leave an audit trail. This map is none of
# those things: each deploy replaces it wholesale, which on 6 September 2026
# revoked three live tokens in turn and left an .env.example placeholder
# granting admin on a public endpoint for ~31 minutes.
#
# It still resolves so a running deployment keeps working mid-migration. Once
# every client holds a credential, set HUB_DISABLE_LEGACY_TOKENS=1, confirm
# nothing broke, then delete the secret.
# HUB_API_TOKENS={"<random-32-bytes>":{"id":"admin","roles":["admin"]}}
# HUB_DISABLE_LEGACY_TOKENS=1
